>> title: Ham Hock Stock
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, stock, southern, smoked, make-ahead
>> counters: Meat and Three
>> aka: smoked pork stock, ham hock broth, smoked pork pot, seasoning meat, pot likker base, smoked turkey stock
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr 30 min
>> slack: forgiving — three hours or four gives the same stock and it is better the next day, which is why it is made three quarts at a time; salt is the part with no room, and it stays out until the end because the hocks are already salty and four sides get built on this
>> pairs-with: collard-greens, green-beans, black-eyed-peas, butter-beans
>> step.1: Cook this once and four sides come out of it. The greens, the green beans, the peas and the butter beans all want this instead of water, so it is worth three quarts at a time.
>> step.2: rinse, into the pot
>> step.3: simmer bare 3 hr, skimmed
>> step.4: strain, pick the meat off the bone

Cook this once and four sides come out of it. The greens, the green beans, the peas and the butter beans all want this instead of water, so it is worth three quarts at a time.

Rinse @smoked ham hocks{2}(about 2 lb / 900 g), @smoked pork neck bones{1%lb}(450 g) and lay them in a #stockpot{}.

Simmer @&(~1)smoked pork{} with @cold water{4%qt}(3.8 L), @yellow onion{1%large}(halved), @garlic{6%cloves}(smashed), @bay leaves{2}, @black peppercorns{1%tsp}, @dried red pepper flakes{1/2%tsp} at a bare ~simmer{3%hr}, skimming the grey foam off in the first ten minutes.

Strain @&(~1)pot{} through a #fine sieve{} and pick the meat off the bone.

Stir the picked meat back into whichever pot this stock goes into. Salt is for the end, not now, because the hocks are already salty and three hours of simmering concentrates them.
